{"id": "EUVD-2026-96430", "enisaUuid": "50c05544-e7b2-3bdd-b863-fa57ac5ec3ba", "description": "Tabularis through 0.27.0 contains an incorrect authorization vulnerability in the MCP run_query safety gate that allows prompt-injected agents or untrusted MCP clients to bypass read-only mode by submitting side-effecting SELECT statements. Attackers can run statements like SELECT setval, nextval, or PostgreSQL query_to_xml with embedded DELETE to modify data without approval prompts.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T19:54:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T11:49:10", "baseScore": 5.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind/S1BofaIsMx", "https://github.com/TabularisDB/tabularis/blob/804c4c3bb6fd8eaa2e36cbe49f6c0d58f373b5e9/src-tauri/src/ai_activity.rs#L357-L416", "https://github.com/TabularisDB/tabularis/blob/804c4c3bb6fd8eaa2e36cbe49f6c0d58f373b5e9/src-tauri/src/mcp/mod.rs#L1136-L1171", "https://github.com/TabularisDB/tabularis", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/tabularis-through-0.27.0-read-only-bypass-via-mcp-run-query-select-classification"], "aliases": ["GHSA-jj9h-m6r9-g37h", "CVE-2026-108604"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f24e7831-3cde-3eb1-84cc-7b9205440da0", "product": {"name": "tabularis", "vendor": {"name": "TabularisDB"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.27.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bd655db2-63be-366c-9c9c-e771c6b0319c", "vendor": {"name": "TabularisDB"}}], "isExploited": false}